## Politics and administration
### Cultural events and festivals
[![Image 51](https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Universitatea_de_Medicin%C4%83_%C5%9Fi_Farmacie_%22Grigore_T._Popa%22.jpg/250px-Universitatea_de_Medicin%C4%83_%C5%9Fi_Farmacie_%22Grigore_T._Popa%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Universitatea_de_Medicin%C4%83_%C5%9Fi_Farmacie_%22Grigore_T._Popa%22.jpg)
[University of Medicine and Pharmacy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grigore_T._Popa_University_of_Medicine_and_Pharmacy "Grigore T. Popa University of Medicine and Pharmacy")
*   [Alexandru Ioan Cuza University](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexandru_Ioan_Cuza_University "Alexandru Ioan Cuza University")- situated in Copou, is the oldest higher education institution in Romania;  
*   [Gheorghe Asachi Technical University](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gheorghe_Asachi_Technical_University_of_Ia%C5%9Fi "Gheorghe Asachi Technical University of Iaşi") – the school with the oldest engineering tradition in Romania;  
*   [Grigore T. Popa University of Medicine and Pharmacy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grigore_T._Popa_University_of_Medicine_and_Pharmacy "Grigore T. Popa University of Medicine and Pharmacy") – one of the oldest medicine schools in Romania;  
*   [George Enescu National University of Arts](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Enescu_National_University_of_Arts "George Enescu National University of Arts") – the oldest tradition in music and arts education in Romania;  
*   [Ion Ionescu de la Brad University of Life Sciences](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ia%C8%99i_University_of_Life_Sciences "Iași University of Life Sciences") – one of the oldest schools of its kind.

## Politics and administration
### Cultural events and festivals
*   [FC Politehnica Iași](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FC_Politehnica_Ia%C8%99i_(1945) "FC Politehnica Iași (1945)") of the [Romanian football league system](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romanian_football_league_system "Romanian football league system") from 1945 to 2010;  
*   [FC Constructorul Iași](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FC_Constructorul_Ia%C8%99i_(1949)?action=edit&redlink=1 "FC Constructorul Iași (1949) (page does not exist)") of the Romanian football league system from 1952 to 1995;  
*   Clubul Sportiv Armata Iași of the Republican Basketball Championship (from 1950);[[97]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ia%C8%99i#cite_note-97)  
*   ACS Penicilina Iași of the [Divizia A1 (women's volleyball)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Divizia_A1_(women's_volleyball) "Divizia A1 (women's volleyball)") (from 1962);  
*   Terom Iași of the [Liga Națională (women's handball)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liga_Na%C8%9Bional%C4%83_(women's_handball) "Liga Națională (women's handball)") (from 1983 to 2012);  
*   Politehnica Național Iași of the [Liga Națională (women's basketball)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liga_Na%C8%9Bional%C4%83_(women's_basketball) "Liga Națională (women's basketball)") (until 2017).

